{{Source status|status=V2 architectural working doctrine|note=Defines how BITwiki V2 should recover, understand, mature, and integrate V1 design signal without flattening its voice or confusing historical design intent with implemented capability.}}

= V1 maturation doctrine =

'''V1 gave BITwiki its imagination. V2 gives that imagination a coherent substrate.'''

BITwiki V1 was both a working MediaWiki implementation and a much larger conceptual experiment. Its writings described sophisticated ontology, epistemics, confidence systems, templates, schemas, modules, relationships, portals, transclusion, semantic organization, composable Book Matter, knowledge graphs, research workflows, and human–AI knowledge production. The deployed implementation realized only part of that design space.

That difference is not treated as failure or as permission to discard the earlier work. V1 functioned as prototype, design notebook, philosophical source, schema experiment, and testbed. Some ideas were implemented, some were only partially realized, some remained design intent, some failed under use, and some now have better technical primitives available.

V2 therefore does not begin by rewriting V1. It begins by recovering its signal.

== Maturation principle ==

'''V1 → preserve → understand → identify signal → mature primitive → enhance → integrate into V2.'''

# '''Preserve''' — retain exact public source, revision history, authored language, provenance, and historical branches.
# '''Understand''' — determine what the text, template, category, property, workflow, or architectural proposal was actually trying to accomplish.
# '''Identify signal''' — separate durable insight from incidental syntax, implementation constraint, duplication, abandoned scaffolding, and historical residue.
# '''Mature primitive''' — express the surviving function using the narrowest coherent V2 primitive: page, namespace, entity type, domain, property, relationship, template, Book Matter, transclusion, query, portal, graph, workflow, research object, or another justified mechanism.
# '''Enhance''' — use present MediaWiki capabilities, extensions, agent workflows, source control, semantic querying, structured research, and external tooling to achieve what V1 could only partially express.
# '''Integrate''' — connect the mature primitive into the V2 ontology, epistemics, navigation, provenance, knowledge lifecycle, and human–AI research system without recreating V1's conflations.

== Two V1s must be distinguished ==

=== V1 as implemented system ===
The historical public wiki provides direct evidence of what actually existed: authored pages, revisions, category memberships, implemented templates, semantic annotations, redirects, and other deployed MediaWiki objects. Those facts must not be inflated by later interpretation.

=== V1 as design imagination ===
The V1 corpus also contains specifications, wanted templates, philosophical writings, proposed ontologies, schemas, modularity experiments, research concepts, and architectural ambitions that were not fully implemented.

'''Design intent is not implementation evidence. It is nevertheless valuable design evidence.'''

V2 should preserve both and label the distinction clearly:
* implemented capability is historical fact;
* proposed capability is design lineage;
* partial implementation is an experiment to evaluate;
* superseded machinery may still contain durable signal;
* strong authored work may remain canonical or near-canonical even when its surrounding schema changes.

== Harmony, not replacement ==

The objective is not to normalize BITwiki into a conventional encyclopedia.

V1's strongest work includes a distinct systems-oriented, cryptopunk, post-digital, post-scarcity, human–AI research voice. The Manifesto, Charter lineage, philosophical writings, and other foundational texts should not be stripped of that character merely to make them resemble institutional policy prose.

'''Preserve the vision. Preserve the voice. Preserve the intellectual experiments. Improve the machinery.'''

Epistemic rigor should support visionary writing by making source, interpretation, speculation, uncertainty, disagreement, and implementation status inspectable. It should not sterilize the writing that gives the project direction.

== From imagined capability to mature capability ==

{| class="wikitable"
! V1 design signal !! Historical implementation question !! V2 maturation question
|-
| Ontology || What types, topics, categories, semantic annotations, and proposed schemas actually existed? || Which meanings belong to Entity type, Domain, Category, Relationship, property families, or specialized ontologies?
|-
| Epistemics || Which confidence, uncertainty, provenance, review, evidence, and skepticism mechanisms were actually implemented versus described? || How should epistemic status, confidence rationale, provenance, evidence structures, review, uncertainty, and confidence trails interoperate?
|-
| Confidence systems || Was confidence encoded numerically, structurally, rhetorically, through sources, or only proposed? || Preserve the confidence-trail concept as traversable justification rather than forcing one universal score.
|-
| Templates || Which templates were implemented, called, wanted, unused, or merely discussed? || What small reusable template families provide real behavior without turning every concept into premature schema?
|-
| Book Matter || Which modular sections or content atoms were authored and transcluded? || How can coherent canonical pages expose reusable sections, subobjects, transclusions, and progressive disclosure without fragmentation?
|-
| Transclusion || Where was reuse actually operational? || Treat transclusion as a first-class composition mechanism for human and agent retrieval.
|-
| Semantic properties || Which properties existed in annotations or authored Property pages? || Give each property one semantic job, explicit value expectations, and validation where useful.
|-
| Relationships || Which graph relations were implemented and which were conceptual? || Use the strongest honest relation supported by evidence; expand relation families from demonstrated need.
|-
| Portals || Which portals or subject gateways existed and how were they used? || Build domain and cross-domain orientation surfaces backed by semantic queries and curated navigation.
|-
| Categories || What jobs did V1 categories perform simultaneously? || Retain categories primarily as human browse/index surfaces while moving ontology, type, status, provenance, and lifecycle to dedicated primitives.
|-
| Knowledge graphs || What graph behavior was actually queryable? || Generate graph views from explicit semantic relations and provenance rather than treating visual linkage as ontology by itself.
|-
| Modules / schemas || Which modules and schema concepts performed executable work? || Introduce computational or schema machinery only when recurring behavior and validation justify it.
|-
| Research system || How were papers, patents, hypotheses, experiments, datasets, tools, and research outputs represented? || Mature BITwiki into a laboratory-grade research substrate connecting literature, patents, claims, evidence, methods, experiments, datasets, implementations, people, organizations, and resulting knowledge.
|-
| Human–AI knowledge production || Which agent, BIThub, BITCORE, and authorship concepts were operational at the time? || Make the knowledge continuum explicit: live work → cognition/research → artifacts → review → durable semantic knowledge → reuse.
|}

This table is a research framework, not a declaration that every imagined V1 object must become a V2 feature.

== Architectural constraint ==

V2 can safely recover ambitious V1 capabilities only because its base dimensions are being separated.

'''Namespace ≠ entity type ≠ domain ≠ category ≠ Book Matter ≠ epistemic standing ≠ lifecycle ≠ relationship ≠ navigation view.'''

A mature primitive should have one primary job. Multiple views may be generated from the same underlying semantics, but the system should not overload one field merely because it is convenient.

== A laboratory, not only an encyclopedia ==

The mature direction extends beyond reference pages. BITwiki can support a full research environment using MediaWiki and its extensions together with source control, SSO, BIThub, BITCORE, semantic queries, forms, graphs, citation systems, structured datasets, agent workflows, and external research tooling.

Potential research objects include claims and hypotheses; publications and references; patents and prior art; datasets; methods and protocols; experiments and observations; models and theories; implementations and software; instruments and materials; people and organizations; projects and laboratories; evidence for and against claims; replication and validation records; and research artifacts and generated analyses.

These should not be created as a giant schema in advance. V1 signal and real V2 corpus needs should determine which objects deserve first-class representation.

== Migration questions ==

For every significant V1 primitive or family, ask:
# What exact public source and revisions establish its lineage?
# What was actually implemented?
# What was proposed but never implemented?
# What problem was the design trying to solve?
# Which parts survived contact with use?
# Which parts were artifacts of the old implementation?
# Does V2 already have a primitive for the durable function?
# Is the current V2 primitive too weak to preserve the original signal?
# Can current MediaWiki capabilities and ecosystem tooling realize the idea more cleanly?
# What evidence would justify expanding the schema?
# What authored language or philosophical lineage must remain intact?
# How should the resulting capability be validated?

== Maturation register ==

Before implementing large new schema families, major V1 concepts should be entered into a maturation register with: V1 primitive; source lineage; historical state; durable signal; V1 limitation; existing V2 primitive; proposed maturation; integration points; validation; and status.

The register prevents V2 from confusing enthusiasm with implementation and prevents cleanup from accidentally deleting future-facing design signal.

== Success condition ==

V2 succeeds when the imaginative range of V1 can return through cleaner primitives without returning to structural ambiguity.

'''The objective is to make the original vision more executable, inspectable, composable, and durable than it was before.'''

